    "number": 36889,
    "state": "open",
    "locked": false,
    "maintainer_can_modify": true,
    "title": "cmake: Switch `include_directories` -> `target_include_directories`",
    "user": {
      "login": "hebasto",
      "id": 32963518,
      "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjMyOTYzNTE4",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32963518?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/hebasto",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/hebasto",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hebasto/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hebasto/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hebasto/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hebasto/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hebasto/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hebasto/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hebasto/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hebasto/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hebasto/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "Use of non-target directives is not recommended. As of CMake 4.5.0, it triggers `-Wnon-target-directive` warnings:\n```console\n$ cmake -B build -Wnon-target-directive\n<snip>\nCMake Warning (non-target-directive) at src/CMakeLists.txt:8 (include_directories):\n  Use of non-target directives is not recommended.  Consider\n  target_include_directories instead.\nThis warning is for project developers.  Use -Wno-author or\n-Wno-non-target-directive to suppress it.\n\n<snip>\n```\n\nOur custom [check](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/blob/29f7e30d547c30ddb7a637bc3a2dbc7c0e3f5469/CMakeLists.txt#L744-L745) does not cover the `src/` subdirectory.\n\nOnce one of the CI jobs runs CMake >=4.5.0, that custom check can be removed.\n\nThe counterpart for the `secp256k1` repo is [here](https://github.com/bitcoin-core/secp256k1/pull/1996).",
    "labels": [
      {
        "id": 61889416,
        "node_id": "MDU6TGFiZWw2MTg4OTQxNg==",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bitcoin/bitcoin/labels/Build%20system",
